            <ArticleTitle>[Experience in the use of needle peripheral venous catheters in children].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>59-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The use of peripheral venous catheters manufactured by Johnson &amp; Johnson Medical Ltd. in children was evaluated in terms of painfulness of venipuncture and cannulation, number of attempts needed to succeed, convenience of handling, and duration of the cannulation period. The intravenous catheters of Johnson &amp; Johnson Medical Ltd. minimized the pain of venipuncture and cannulation and proved to be safe and convenient for patients and nursing staff.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
